session:pr503Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #157 originally bundled six deferred Manchester Syntax grammar productions (SWRL Rule: frames, DisjointUnionOf:/HasKey:, SubPropertyChain:, compound data ranges, Datatype: frame) as one follow-up to #139. That's too much for a single PR to review meaningfully, so the work was scoped down to DisjointUnionOf: only -- chosen first because ClassAxiom::DisjointUnion(Vec<Annotation>, Class, Vec<ClassExpression>) already existed in owl_ontology::axioms (confirmed by reading axioms.rs before writing any tests against it), so no data-model design was needed, only grammar/parser work. The parser change mirrors the existing Class: frame section pattern (SubClassOf:/EquivalentTo:/DisjointWith: in frame.rs's class_section), but the W3C grammar for DisjointUnionOf: is 'annotations description2List' -- a single leading Annotations: block followed by a plain comma list, not the per-item-annotated list form SubClassOf:/EquivalentTo:/DisjointWith: use. That matches the shape misc's EquivalentClasses:/DisjointClasses: already used, so the existing opt_annotations helper was reused rather than annotated_list, keeping the new section consistent with sibling code instead of inventing a third annotation-handling pattern. serialize.rs's prior log_skip(\"DisjointUnionOf: (#157)\") was replaced with real emission, verified via a round-trip test. The other five deferred items were each filed as independent GitHub issues (#498-#502, with #502 noted as depending on #501) rather than left as prose in this issue, per this repo's CLAUDE.md rule that deferred scope must become real trackable issues." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:503 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr503 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
